{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463993-taft\u00e2ni-and-djinn","id":1463993,"title":"Taft\u00e2ni and djinn","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-15T03:19:26-07:00","id":1463993,"title":"Taft\u00e2ni and djinn","content":"I've been reading through lost paths about how the Taftani bind djinn to a bottle. But I can't seem to find anything on how they control the djinn now that they're entrapped. It makes it quite clear that the djinn is likely to flee once the bottle is opened. So how do djinn work as their slaves?<br /> <br /> Because usually to compel a spirit is spirit 4. but the djinn bottle is spirit 3. have I just missed something in the book? Do they entrap them and then converse with them in the bottle for a deal to earn their freedom?? but surely they can't do that for all the tiny lesser djinn?<br /> <br /> I have scanned through the book so it's possible I missed something <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25510-jasper-mage","name":"Jasper mage","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T04:48:59-07:00","id":1464002,"title":"","content":"Well in the original stories that I remember the Djinn weren't compelled to help whomever let them out. Sometimes they did out of gratitude, but I remember one specific story where the djinn grew so bitter over the centuries of his imprisonment that he vowed to kill whomever let him out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T11:08:09-07:00","id":1464056,"title":"","content":"Ramnesis is right about the old stories. Still the binding that locks the djinni in the bottle let's the Mage blackmail the djinni in question into oaths of service and obedience. The skills used to make such an oath aren't magical, they are logical and legalistic. The mage must bind the djinni with promises the djinni can't risk breaking. Failure to clearly understand the Code of Solomon can lead to oaths that the djinni can simply ignore or repudiate. Poor wording or weak logic can also give the djinni loopholes to escape through as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T16:26:04-07:00","id":1464102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1463993-taft\u00e2ni-and-djinn?p=1464056#post1464056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ramnesis is right about the old stories. Still the binding that locks the djinni in the bottle let's the Mage blackmail the djinni in question into oaths of service and obedience. The skills used to make such an oath aren't magical, they are logical and legalistic. The mage must bind the djinni with promises the djinni can't risk breaking. Failure to clearly understand the Code of Solomon can lead to oaths that the djinni can simply ignore or repudiate. Poor wording or weak logic can also give the djinni loopholes to escape through as well.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Good tie-in for an Akashic Brotherhood, Shi-Ren NPC. They are very legalistic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}